    "result_text": "Creating an owner now writes an audit line to the `AUDIT` logger with the owner id, customer code and registration date. The full test suite passes (Maven exited with 0), including the new audit test.\n\nThe change is in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`: once the owner is saved, it logs at INFO level, for example:\n\n```\nINFO  AUDIT - Owner created: id=11, customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001, registrationDate=2026-10-14\n```\n\nI put the line in the controller's create method rather than in `ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`, because `saveOwner` also handles updates and only creates should be audited. It logs after the save, so the id and customer code are already set and failed creates aren't logged.",
